session: rebase-four-branches

## Task
Rebase all four TA 0.9 branches onto the current upstream `main`
(`aa86a2a9` — "fix(saturation): log actual analyzer mode ... (#1334)"), which is
2 commits ahead of the shared base `f5b7577c`. Do this one worktree at a time
via `EnterWorktree` (never `cd` / `git checkout` to switch). Dean has directed
that you (the ta-veto-liveness coder) handle all four in a single session.

A `git merge-tree` simulation already confirms **all four rebase clean — no
conflicts expected on any branch.** If any branch does hit a conflict, stop and
write a `plan__*.md` handoff rather than improvising a resolution.

## Branches / worktrees (all off `main@f5b7577c`)
- `ta-devguide-fixes`       → worktree `../ta-devguide-fixes`
- `ta-registration-safety`  → worktree `../ta-registration-safety`
- `ta-model-level-demand`   → worktree `../ta-model-level-demand`
- `ta-veto-liveness`        → worktree `../ta-veto-liveness`

## Per branch
1. `EnterWorktree` the branch's worktree; verify with `pwd` + `git branch --show-current`.
2. `git fetch upstream`
3. `git rebase upstream/main`
4. Gates: `make test`, `gofmt -l ./internal/... ./pkg/... ./cmd/...`, `make lint`,
   `go build ./...` (add `-race` for `ta-veto-liveness` per its prior runs).
5. Verify DCO sign-off survived: `git log upstream/main..HEAD --format="%b" | grep Signed-off-by`.

## Additional for `ta-model-level-demand` only — reword two commit subjects
These two subjects carry internal review-finding tags that are meaningless in
upstream history and must be stripped (descriptive prose only):
- `throughput: weight model-level avgOL by replica count (review F1)`
  → `throughput: weight model-level avgOL by replica count`
- `docs(multi-analyzer-pipeline): add ArrivalRate to AnalyzerInput field table (review F2)`
  → `docs(multi-analyzer-pipeline): add ArrivalRate to AnalyzerInput field table`
Do the reword in the same interactive rebase. Preserve the `Signed-off-by`
trailer on both (verify with the grep in step 5).

## Do NOT push
Per coder rules, do not `git push` (these would be force-pushes; Dean runs them).
When all four are rebased and green, write a `plan__*.md` handoff reporting: the
new tip SHA per branch, gates-green confirmation per branch, and the reworded C
subjects. Dean force-pushes the four branches; PRs are then created on the clean
tips.
